'''Gran País del Nord''' ({{Literal translation|big north country}}; {{Lang-arn|Reipún-ko|lit=shaked waters}}), colloquially known as '''Gran País''', '''Gran Nord''' or simply '''GPN''' is a [[W:Bioregionalism|bio]], [[Megaregions of Balisca|geographic and cultural region]] that generally comprises the regions of [[Cerdanya]] that are north of the [[Matarrañya / Cañadapirén]]. Spanning the region's 37 constituent [[Cantons of Balisca|cantons]], its main population centers form the [[Mercepción|''Mercepción'' area]] (anchored by the cities of [[Concepción]] and [[Merced]]).

Gran Nord is just one emergent megalopolis (also known as a megaregion) of eight such territories in the [[Baliscan Confederation]]. Half of the nation's population growth and two-thirds of its economic growth are expected to occur within those regions over the next four decades.

Today, {{W|tourism}} (especially {{W|ecotourism}}) has become a substantial driver of economic activity in Gran Nord, with smaller sectors including {{W|pisciculture}}, manufacturing, and Arctic logistics.

Despite its increasingly urban character, it is one of Balisca's most ecologically important [[W:Biogeographic realm|biogeographic realms]], providing key ecosystem services such as filtering pollutants and sediments from the rivers and supporting a number of endangered species. The region is also known for the complexity of its landforms, the result of millions of years of tectonic plate movements. Because Gran País is crossed by six major earthquake faults, the region is particularly exposed to hazards presented by large earthquakes (such as [[W:landslide|landslides]] and {{W|tsunamis}}). The region is heavily affected by the [[Arctic Circumpolar Current]], and has a {{W|Marine west coast (Cfb)}} climate, and is ideal for outdoor recreational and athletic activities such as hiking.

